            <ArticleTitle>[Endotoxin aggression in the development of hemostatic disorders in children with surgical diseases].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>32-7</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The role of endotoxin aggression in the development of hemostatic disorders was analyzed in 62 children who had undergone urgent and elective surgeries. It is demonstrated that indices of endotoxin-antiendotoxin system and hemostasis before surgery may be regarded as prognostic criteria for development of complications during and after surgery.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
